{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle. The key constraint is \"the award itself was originally created in the 2000s.\" The Booker Prize (1969) doesn't fit, but the Man Booker International Prize was inaugurated in 2005. However, Obioma's books were shortlisted for the regular Booker Prize, not the International one.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about a different award entirely. Let me think about awards created in the 2000s and look at the structure differently. Perhaps Book A is a contender for an award created in the 2000s, and in the year Book A was published, Book B won that same award. Let me look at the Man Booker International Prize winners in the 2010s and find a book translated into 25+ languages that was a contender.\n\nLet me check the 2019 Man Booker International Prize winner and shortlist, and also reconsider whether the puzzle might involve the regular Booker Prize with a different interpretation.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Booker International Prize 2019 winner Celestial Bodies Jokha Alharthi\", \"International Booker Prize 2018 Flights Olga Tokarczuk winner\", \"Man Booker International Prize 2017 winner Love in the Time of Cholera\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_c55644fd7b1e48798487e4df","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"book translated 25 languages shortlisted International Booker Prize 2010s\", \"novel translated over 25 languages contender Man Booker International Prize\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_bace400983d04c2ca3defa68","index":1,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789472936,"id":"chatcmpl-7165ded8-f36e-9f06-a967-f404219b6015","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":19459,"completion_tokens":301,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":19760,"cached_tokens":3328,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3328},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost